; BOUNCE BONANZA - the VICTORY fanfare (SPEC.md 137.22.9): the finish sequence's
; tune, played over its 2 s (BZ_FIN_STEPS = 110 sub-ticks) in the course song's
; place.  C major at 164 BPM - a 16th is a row of FIVE sub-ticks - two
; patterns of 11 rows, exactly 110 sub-ticks of sound:
;   A  the trumpet climbs a C triad: g c e G(dotted) e g, then C held
;   B  IV - V - I: f a c d b, and the C held to the last sub-tick
; and a third pattern of nothing, which `loop` points at: the song does NOT
; repeat, it ends in silence (the same shape 137.23's `attract` plans).
; On the speaker the lead is the whole tune (the bass only where it rests).

song victory "Victory"
groove 5
unit 16
rows 11
spkbass
voice lead trumpet
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord stab

lead LA = o4 v14 l16 g o5 c e g8 e16 g16 c4 |
lead LB = o5 v14 l16 f a o6 c d o5 b o6 c4. |
bass BA = o3 l8 c r g r l16 c r c |
bass BB = o3 l16 f r f r g r g r c:3 |
chord CA = o4 [c e g]:3 [c e g]:3 [e g >c]:5 |
chord CB = o4 [f a >c]:3 [g b >d]:2 [e g >c]:6 |
drum DA = l16 k r k r s s s s k8 r |
drum DB = l16 s s s s t T k4 r |

order LA BA CA DA
order LB BB CB DB
order - - - -
loop 2
